{"title":"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_(Quick_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 (Quick and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In some countries, automobile fuel efficiency is measured in liters per <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> kilometers while other countries use miles per gallon. Suppose that 1 kilometer equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> miles, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gallon equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> liters. Which of the following gives the fuel efficiency in liters per <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> kilometers for a car that gets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> miles per gallon?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/c/90cbfc1376055731afa4a5a74e561738556b76e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{x}{100lm} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } \\frac{xlm}{100} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } \\frac{lm}{100x} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } \\frac{100}{xlm} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } \\frac{100lm}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"530\" height=\"39\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The formula for fuel efficiency is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/e/90eeec553fea9ce3012153b8582c2d9f6a593332.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Gas Consumption}}.\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"39\" />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mile equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7ae85451a1c19c8cae1d5f6323b65038f43c6eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 1m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"38\" /> kilometers. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/c/60c6bc79b632eb92edc1ac2b7389e21da8beb47b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x\\text{ miles}}{1\\text{ gallon}} = \\frac{\\frac{x}{m}\\text{ kilometers}}{l\\text{ liters}} = \\frac{1\\text{ kilometer}}{\\frac{lm}{x}\\text{ liters}} = \\frac{100\\text{ kilometers}}{\\frac{100lm}{x}\\text{ liters}}.\\]\" width=\"433\" height=\"45\" />\nTherefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0accfbed6b9883719cfac55f34f8ce9a5e0517b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{100lm}{x}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"105\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since it can be a bit odd to think of \"liters per <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> km\", this statement's numerical value is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> km per <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> liter:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> km  requires <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> liters, so the numerator is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> liters is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gallon, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> miles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gallon, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/a/b8a605b10d0ccf55779a1811f1f253aa95223414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\text{ liter} = \\frac{x}{l}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"85\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the requested expression is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/d/1bdc2499160b98f3241939802fcf4b77f1500b3b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[100\\cdot\\frac{m}{(\\frac{x}{l})} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{100lm}{x}}.\\]\" width=\"194\" height=\"50\" />\n-Benedict T (countmath1)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A car that gets a gallon for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> miles has a fuel efficiency of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/619a7a43533270c3a353bb19185bc19df0397f11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1 \\text{ gallon}}{x\\text{ miles}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" /> We want to convert these units to liters and kilometers. Since one gallon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> liters, that can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daa5c15a8d6fa97ea42f9a98ad965e403c73f8be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{l \\text{ liters}}{x\\text{ miles}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>Now to convert the miles into kilometers. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> km is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> miles, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mile is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/4659ee9ed51157f75502b0ceabc4b396eccd39ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"38\" /> km. Plug that in to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/b/34b0c9f5f64582bd6c6e2168b16eef403f1d5828.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{l \\text{ liter}}{x * \\frac{1}{m} \\text{ km}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"82\" height=\"46\" /> Simplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/673b3747209344f359ffbff6efc3a4d7be1fdb7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{lm \\text{ liters}}{x \\text{ km}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>But the problem asked for the fuel efficiency of liters per <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> km, not just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> km. So instead of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, we put in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/4/6944ddad02e9832cbf3c8e56dcd7ea934cce9cf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, getting \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/d/46d745aa70a3de3e7b13426a779b908c3b0c7723.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{100lm}{x}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"100\" height=\"50\" /> as the answer.\n</p><p>~mihikamishra\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_.28Quick_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_(Quick_and_Easy)\">Video Solution 1 (Quick and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 (Quick and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/JX4u3V2IqY0\">https://youtu.be/JX4u3V2IqY0</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/qACAjp1HSxA\">https://youtu.be/qACAjp1HSxA</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A\">2022 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017033026\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.110 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 302/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2320/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 154/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7280/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.029      1 -total\n 59.93%    7.808      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 39.08%    5.092      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:23259:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017033026 and revision id 249440. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}